Z||000012||Mach10||12-21-2001||02:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Blacktree:<BR><B>I've been doing something similar for some time now. But I've added a little twist. <P>First of all, let me explain that these companies are billed for postage when you send back their prepaid postage envelopes. So if you make that envelope nice and heavy, they get charged out the wazoo for postage. So here's what I do: I take pieces of scrap wood, sheet metal, etc (nothing pointed or sharp that could hurt anyone) and wrap them in paper. I cram as much scrap as possible into the envelope, until it's about to burst at the seams. <P>When they have to pay first-class postage on a one-pound envelope, it makes them think twice about sending me anything again.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Just a heads-up... That's MAIL FRAUD... You can get drilled HARDCORE for that... Misuse of the postal service is a felony, last I heard... <P>btw... What is "Homo Sapiens Americanus?" Don't believe I've ever heard that one... <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000013||BN Boomer||12-21-2001||03:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B><BR>Just a heads-up... That's MAIL FRAUD... You can get drilled HARDCORE for that... Misuse of the postal service is a felony, last I heard... <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is that just a Canadian thing? I don't think they could do much to you about that down here in the land of the free. It's certainly not fraud.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Blacktree||12-21-2001||04:03 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>btw... What is "Homo Sapiens Americanus?" Don't believe I've ever heard that one...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>homo sapiens = human<BR>americanus = American<BR>get it?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>BTW, in America it's not considered mail fraud to mail a heavy letter to someone. If I wanted to stick a bar of lead in an envelope and mail it, the US Post Office won't care as long as the postage is paid for and there are no hazardous materials inside. In the above case, it just so happens that someone else is paying the postage. <P>The companies that send out those prepaid-postage envelopes have agreed in advance to pay for the postage, although the envelopes have yet to be mailed and the postage has yet to actually be paid. The post office sends them a bill based on how many envelopes were mailed. The companies just ASSUME that they will be charged the minimal rate on these envelopes.<P>Now if you were to alter the mailing address printed on the envelope (i.e. the address of the company that sent you the junk mail), THAT would be mail fraud.<p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierospeeder||12-21-2001||04:27 AM||||when doing this, it would be a bad idea to put flour in the envelope||||reg||1
Z||000016||rogergarrison||12-21-2001||06:08 AM||||Ive been doing that for years, and police have yet to come. I make sure my name IS in there, I want them to know who it comes from so theyll stop sending it. Ive even heard of people wrapping up bricks and attaching it to the prepaid envelope since they pay by the weight of mail. I guess the post office caught onto that and stopped it though. Id suggest due to recent events, NOT to include any kind of white powders, that could bite you.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Oreif||12-21-2001||08:21 AM||||Usually I get 2 or 3 Credit card applications. I just swap them. So they know what the other company is offering. Geico usually gets AD's from dealerships that have "special sales" so that they can contact the dealer. Mortgage re-finance places get realtor AD's. <P>I feel this helps business for them. Of course now I will have to use a piece of wood inside so the AD's don't get crushed or wrinkled.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||MinnGreenGT||12-21-2001||09:34 AM||||This is fun!  I'm going to stop throwing away all my junk mail... good to know that there are some good idea's for "getting back" at the junk mail people!<P>Thanks for the tip!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
